---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Container from "../components/Container.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="An architect's perspective on enterprise AI — what I work on, why, and how I think about the next decade of transformation."
>
  <article class="bg-paper">
    <Container width="prose" class="py-20 sm:py-28">

      <p class="eyebrow mb-7">About</p>

      <h1
        class="font-[family-name:var(--font-display)] font-extrabold text-[length:var(--text-h1)] tracking-[-0.015em] leading-[1.1] text-[var(--color-ink)] mb-12"
      >
        I help organisations build AI systems that survive contact with reality.
      </h1>

      <div class="space-y-7 prose-serif">
        <p>
          I'm <strong>Aleksandrs Graholskis</strong> — an enterprise AI
          architect working with senior transformation leaders, CIOs, and
          governance functions in mid-to-large organisations across Europe.
        </p>
        <p>
          My focus is the part of the AI lifecycle most teams skip: the
          architecture that decides whether a successful prototype becomes
          a production system or quietly accumulates as
          <em>AI Debt</em>.
          Shadow assistants, ungoverned RAG pipelines, agentic workflows
          built on assumptions no one wrote down. The cost compounds
          silently — until something visible breaks.
        </p>
        <p>
          I work end-to-end on this: AI Debt assessment, governance design
          aligned to the EU AI Act, reference architectures for retrieval
          and agentic systems, and the operating model that makes the
          whole thing maintainable past the launch press release.
        </p>
        <p>
          The longer narrative — origin story, what I've built, why I left
          the obvious career path — lives here in v0.2. For now, the most
          honest representation of how I think is in the
          <a class="underline decoration-[var(--color-amber)] underline-offset-4 text-[var(--color-ink)]" href="/lab">Lab</a>.
          Start there.
        </p>
      </div>

      <hr class="my-16 border-[var(--color-rule)]" />

      <p class="label mb-4">Currently</p>
      <p class="font-[family-name:var(--font-serif)] text-[17px] leading-[1.6] text-[var(--color-ink)]">
        Agentic workflows for procurement and operations ·
        Open to a small number of advisory engagements in 2026 ·
        Based between Riga and Copenhagen.
      </p>

    </Container>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
